Granny, you wouldn't do no harm to give it a try?

19:05.960 --> 19:08.960
A lot of things are different out here.

19:08.960 --> 19:12.960
Well, I'll fish on it for a spell.

19:12.960 --> 19:14.960
Take this.

19:14.960 --> 19:16.960
It's like a whale.

19:16.960 --> 19:19.960
Who said there ain't fish in here?

19:19.960 --> 19:21.960
Well, that's the purgiest I ever seen.

19:21.960 --> 19:23.960
I got you, you rascal.

19:23.960 --> 19:27.960
I'm going to throw you right in the frying pan.

19:27.960 --> 19:30.960
This thing ain't nothing but skin.

19:30.960 --> 19:32.960
That's your Beverly Hills for you.

19:32.960 --> 19:34.960
All flashy and show on the outside

19:34.960 --> 19:40.960
and nothing on the inside where it counts.

19:40.960 --> 19:43.960
Fishing, people, is two different things.

19:43.960 --> 19:46.960
We're going to call in on our neighbors,

19:46.960 --> 19:48.960
and then we'll do our judging.

19:48.960 --> 19:56.960
Well, let's see now.

19:56.960 --> 19:58.960
Which neighbor should we call on first?

19:58.960 --> 20:01.960
Mr. Dryadale's often bossed with his missus,

20:01.960 --> 20:02.960
so let's go this way.

20:02.960 --> 20:04.960
If you ask me, let's go back that way.

20:04.960 --> 20:06.960
Oh, Granny, you promised.

20:06.960 --> 20:10.960
Come on, everybody, let's go.

20:10.960 --> 20:14.960
You'd rather they give us a mass of pollen or something, Paul?

20:14.960 --> 20:16.960
Or maybe some salted down pasta?

20:16.960 --> 20:24.960
Probably so lie on us.

20:24.960 --> 20:27.960
I'm not expecting anyone, Agnes.

20:27.960 --> 20:34.960
Oh, it's probably just some children playing trick or treat, man.

20:34.960 --> 20:36.960
Hi, ma'am, we're the Clampins.

20:36.960 --> 20:38.960
You got something for us?

20:38.960 --> 20:39.960
Yes, ma'am.

20:39.960 --> 20:41.960
Are you running the digs for this?

20:41.960 --> 20:43.960
Yes, ma'am, we are.

20:43.960 --> 20:50.960
In fact, I don't see how anybody gets through that little door.

20:50.960 --> 20:53.960
Come in.

20:53.960 --> 20:57.960
Come in and shut us down as you folks stay up in the hill.

20:57.960 --> 20:58.960
Well, thank you.

20:58.960 --> 21:01.960
We got a lot of calls to make.

21:01.960 --> 21:03.960
This here is Granny.

21:03.960 --> 21:04.960
Howdy.

21:04.960 --> 21:05.960
Hello.

21:05.960 --> 21:07.960
I'm her daughter, Ellie.

21:07.960 --> 21:08.960
Hope.

21:08.960 --> 21:10.960
And if you, Jethro.

21:10.960 --> 21:11.960
Hello.

21:11.960 --> 21:12.960
And I am Jed.

21:12.960 --> 21:13.960
Hello, Jed.

21:13.960 --> 21:14.960
I'm Agnes.

21:14.960 --> 21:17.960
Just call me Aggy.

21:17.960 --> 21:19.960
Mighty nice place you got here, Aggy.

21:19.960 --> 21:24.960
Oh, shucks, ain't nothing but a heap of bricks, but we call it home.

21:24.960 --> 21:27.960
Well, sure is nice to meet up with you.

21:27.960 --> 21:28.960
Oh, now wait just a minute.

21:28.960 --> 21:29.960
I got something for you.

21:29.960 --> 21:31.960
Wait a second.

21:31.960 --> 21:33.960
Here you go, Granny and Ellie.

21:33.960 --> 21:36.960
That's you and Jethro.

21:36.960 --> 21:38.960
That's you and Jethro.

21:38.960 --> 21:39.960
There.

21:39.960 --> 21:40.960
Thank you.

21:40.960 --> 21:42.960
That's smart and neighborly of you.

21:42.960 --> 21:44.960
You must come and see us sometime.

21:44.960 --> 21:46.960
Yeah, we'll go hunting together.

21:46.960 --> 21:48.960
Hey, Aggy, you like to play football?

21:48.960 --> 21:49.960
Love it.

21:49.960 --> 21:53.960
Well, there's a whole bunch of fellas that plays in the pasture down the way a piece.

21:53.960 --> 21:59.960
And they'd like it just fine if I could bring some more girls along.

21:59.960 --> 22:04.960
I don't think...

22:04.960 --> 22:08.960
Please, can we go out now?

22:08.960 --> 22:09.960
Not yet, children.

22:09.960 --> 22:17.960
Not till it gets dark.

22:17.960 --> 22:26.960
Ain't that the most pitiful thing?

22:26.960 --> 22:27.960
Heart rendering.

22:27.960 --> 22:29.960
Just heart rendering.

22:29.960 --> 22:31.960
Nice looking woman.

22:31.960 --> 22:32.960
Friendly as you please.

22:32.960 --> 22:36.960
But them young'uns is the homeliest I ever seen.

22:36.960 --> 22:39.960
I wonder if she didn't want to come a-calling on us.

22:39.960 --> 22:42.960
Yeah, reckon I'd stay home too if my kids looked like that.

22:42.960 --> 22:47.960
I ain't never gonna say a bad word about nobody.

22:47.960 --> 22:49.960
I know what you mean.

22:49.960 --> 22:50.960
There's the diggy.

22:50.960 --> 22:52.960
There's the house we went to.

22:52.960 --> 22:54.960
They was nice to us, wasn't they?

22:54.960 --> 22:55.960
You're right, Dad.

22:55.960 --> 22:58.960
Hey, listen everybody.

22:58.960 --> 22:59.960
I got an idea.

22:59.960 --> 23:04.960
Let's call up Cousin Pearl and tell her to come on out here.

23:04.960 --> 23:07.960
Uncle Jed, you can't call Ma on the telephone.

23:07.960 --> 23:10.960
Mr. Dryad, you say we can call anybody we had a mind to.

23:10.960 --> 23:12.960
Well Ma, she ain't got no telephone at home.

23:12.960 --> 23:13.960
Don't matter.

23:13.960 --> 23:15.960
She ain't never home no how.

23:15.960 --> 23:16.960
Well, you gotta look at it.

23:16.960 --> 23:23.960
You can't never tell what you can do until you try.

23:23.960 --> 23:33.960
Don't forget to spin the wheel.

23:33.960 --> 23:35.960
Hi there, ma'am.

23:35.960 --> 23:39.960
I want to talk to Pearl Bodine back in Oxford.

23:39.960 --> 23:40.960
That's right, operator.

23:40.960 --> 23:43.960
J.D. Clampett in Beverly Hills.

23:43.960 --> 23:48.960
Jed's sure gonna be surprised to hear me talking at him on this thing.

23:48.960 --> 23:54.960
Oh, they're ready to make the connection.

23:54.960 --> 23:56.960
Hello!

23:56.960 --> 23:58.960
Dad, is that you, Jed?

23:58.960 --> 23:59.960
You bet you it is.

23:59.960 --> 24:00.960
Hello, Pearl, you old rascal.

24:00.960 --> 24:02.960
What you doing down there?

24:02.960 --> 24:04.960
How's my promise as Eric?

24:04.960 --> 24:07.960
Jed, throw talk in a minute, but first I want to say something.

24:07.960 --> 24:13.960
Ma'am, you gotta come out here to Beverly Hills and bring Jed's ring.

24:13.960 --> 24:17.960
If she can't get her husband out of here, there ain't no hope.

24:17.960 --> 24:38.960
You ain't never seen so many homely young'uns in all your born days.

24:38.960 --> 24:52.880
I've heard that one Yumbo and there's this one vidéo marriage has opened

24:52.880 --> 25:00.880
in there and now it's gonna go through.

25:00.880 --> 25:02.880
Yeah!

25:02.880 --> 25:09.880
.

